  message: "CLOSED done, 2026-09-25 (P2 review, dev e4a47383ab). DONE-AND-NEVER-CLOSED: fixed by 6196148d11 (2026-09-23, \"fix(erlang,elixir): a call is anchored to the function that contains it (INV-mozas)\"), whose message states \"A def head is no longer emitted as a call\". The same commit reports 1,551 lost call sites that were def heads, the population this row measured as 1,435 self-edges on phoenix.\n\nTHE ROW'S MINIMAL REPRO, re-run through `analyze_elixir` with positive controls in the same file:\n    def insert(a, b), do: {a, b}          -> NO edge (was a self-call at its own head line)\n    def go(x), do: insert(x, x)           -> calls go -> insert, line 3   (control: real calls still emit)\n    def rec(0), do: 0 / def rec(n), do: rec(n - 1)\n                                          -> calls rec(5) -> rec(4) and rec(5) -> rec(5), line 5 (genuine recursion still emits; one symbol per clause, as the commit describes)\nSo the non-recursive head self-edge is gone, and real calls and real recursion survive.\n\nNOT re-measured: the phoenix corpus count. The fixture above is the row's own minimal repro."  # 52a6
